**Top Must-fix**: (1) operational "source-attested" definition + wrong-suffix negative test; (2) **measure strictness-induced regressions** (v1-pass→084a-fail) on val 161 + clean 1,617 and classify kinds of all residual failures — today nothing bounds the match-removing direction; (3) distinct typed-slot uniqueness semantics + tests (18일+18명 → no match); (4) freeze verifier/spec hash *before* re-scoring; (5) per-flip clause attribution + "0 expected excluded flips under URL-only"; (6) concrete INCONCLUSIVE rule; (7) human-50 pre-registration as blocking gate.

**Top experiments**: spec-faithful 084a audit + clause ablation (~0.5–1 day impl, minutes compute); strictness exposure census (same run); residual-failure kind taxonomy (~1–2 h); human-50 dry run (~2–3 person-h); full human 50 (12–20 person-h, after pre-registration).

**Key original finding**: 084a's stricter canonicalization can only *remove* matches (the wrap join is the only match-adding change), and the old audit structurally could not detect such regressions — "clean 1,617 diff = 0" is vacuous in the strict direction too. If any regression hits 1,293/2,586, the expected 160s break, and the honest outcome is no candidate with pilot300 fallback intact. D-083 (`selected_step: null`, pilot300 fallback) stands unchanged; nothing here is an approval.
